== Graphics Mods

Light graphical enhancements compatible with Wave 0's vanilla+ philosophy. No gameplay values change.

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/323")[*Neutral LUTs - No Color Filters*]

Replaces the base game's heavy color-grading LUTs with neutral ones, removing the green/teal cast from interiors and the orange cast from many planets for a more natural image.

- *Author:* fadingsignal
- *Version:* 1.5 (updated 2024-10-03)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *Impact:* Color grading only — recommended as the single most effective "looks better" change in Wave 0

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3486")[*Starfield HD Reworked Project*]

High-resolution texture overhaul of environments, characters, and effects while staying faithful to the vanilla art style. Optional here; a 6 GB+ VRAM GPU is recommended to avoid any frame-rate hit.

- *Author:* HalkHogan
- *Version:* 1.0-fix (updated 2023-09-23)
- *Dependencies:* None (requires `bInvalidateOlderFiles=1` from setup)
- *Impact:* Textures only — no gameplay change; old but texture-only, so staleness is weak evidence of breakage
